    {
      "id": "claim_ade60b953f454f95a686e2ea7eae1f75",
      "statement": "CIB 2Q26 net income was $2,740M (down 5.2% sequentially, up 9.2% year-on-year) on net revenue of $8,480M. The sequential decline is driven by Markets revenue falling to $4,610M from a seasonally strong, record-derivatives 1Q26, while investment banking fees rose to $1,820M. Payments revenue was $2.5B and real-time payment volume rose 64%.",
